metal2vulkan: the native 8-bit linear filter wraps its coordinate as Metal does, and PanVK on the Mali-G72 takes it (Scion)

Upstream:  metal2vulkan, https://github.com/steelbrain/metal2vulkan, at 720ef1ce9ae2a2068999a8675717418b9416283e, after
           AdrenoMetal's 16 patches to it and Scion's 0001 to 0011; tools/metal/mk-metal2vulkan.sh applies them in that order,
           then this.
Licence:   GPL-2.0-or-later OR LGPL-3.0-or-later, metal2vulkan's (its LICENSE); this patch is a change to it and under the same
           terms. Nothing of it is in Scion's MIT or APSL files.
Author:    the HakiOS authors (Scion), 15 November 2026.

Why. Metal's linear filter of an 8-bit unorm texture is emulated exactly by default (four fetches and about a thousand
instructions a sample: the class is data, so every format's decode stays in the module). CoreAnimation samples its BGRA8
layers that way, and on the Galaxy S9's Mali-G72 the two window-server shaders that do it cost 11 of the 23 ms the GPU spends
on the home screen's main pass while swiping (docs/metal.md). The native arm (the device's filter at the centre of Metal's
1/256 step, DriverDeviation::Unorm8LinearFilter) is for a device measured within one code of Metal.

What.
- lower/sampler/native.rs: `cell`, the native coordinate, wraps a repeating or mirrored axis's coordinate by position::wrap,
  as Metal does (the subtraction rounded up; down at a power-of-two size), not by the plain f32 subtraction. Where -1 < u < 0
  the plain subtraction rounds to nearest and can cross a step's edge, so the device read the neighbouring step: a weight
  1/256 off, up to one code of contrast. Clamping axes are unchanged. position::wrap is pub(super) for it.
- device/driver_facts.rs: Unorm8LinearFilter measured on PanVK, Mesa 25.0.7, on the Mali-G72 (vendor 0x13b5, device
  0x62210000) by Scion's tools/vk/vk_filter_probe.c: the m2v probe's textures, coordinates and modes, against Metal's filter
  computed exactly from Metal's position rules: 0.89 of a code at most (0.84 clamp to edge, 0.78 clamp to zero); the
  device's blend alone, at the step named, the same. With the old wrap it was 1.35 codes, on repeating and mirrored axes.

The policy that takes the deviation (Unorm8LinearFilterPolicy::DeviceWithinOneCode) is the bridge's
(tools/metal/bridge/NativeMetalObjects.rs).

